o the shoreline by  the dozens uh we talked to one man he  told us he spent twelve thousand dollars  to bring over him his wife and his child  there was an unaccompanied girl only age  10 who came across  completely alone and then take a look at  these photos right here this is what was  on the shoreline as these boats were  coming across there were well over 100  people waiting to be across you can see  it with the thermal vision from the  national guard you can see a second  photo here they're able to watch these  guys during the night as they are coming  across the river and bringing their  human cargo over ask them why they're  not able to arrest them on the shoreline  they say it's a safety issue they're  worried the other smugglers will take it  out on the migrants potentially flip a  raft over and it'll turn into a rescue  operation for a bunch of little kids  take a look at this last piece of video  right here this was remarkable last  night we witnessed automatic gunfire  going from mexico directly into the  united states  the national guard soldiers we were with  you can hear them kind of reacting  saying whoa holy bleep  they say this is  suspected cartel gunfire going  indiscriminately directly into the  united states they said it was going  above one of their observation posts  kind of near the border wall but  incredibly rare to actually see direct  gunfire  from a machine gun going into the u.s  like that this was the second volley i  didn't get my phone out in time for the  first volley but pretty wild to see that  and to wrap it up here the national  guard soldiers told us multiple times in  recent days armed cartel members with  ak-47s have stood on the opposite side  of the rio grande from them and have  taunted them have racked the slides on  their guns and have yelled to them in  spanish that oh we should just shoot you  soldiers so tensions here along the rio  grande along the border obviously going  up and that cartel activity in the city  behind us um  it's still there we'll send it back to  you wow  bill that looked like tracer fire  and if the video is correct from left to  right that would be from south to north  as you described for the mexican side  what would they be firing at  don't know so in past days the soldiers  have told us there have been a ton of  cartel gun fights here in the city  behind us it's called ciudad miguel  aleman one of the most violent cities we  don't know if that gunfire was from a  mexican drug cartel shootout or if they  were just shooting across the border as  an intimidation factor above one of the  observation posts we don't know but  you're correct that was tracer gunfire  you can see the red tracers and  typically that's every few rounds is  when you see one of those tracers but  the soldiers told us they suspect it was  from an m240 machine gun or potentially  because the tracers were so slow it was  potentially a 50 caliber machine gun so  they don't know exactly but you can kind  of hear the reaction of the soldiers in  the background watching it with us they  were pretty shocked to see that it's a  remarkable report bill malugan back in  the border today thank you bill for that  careful what they wish for because they  might get a response i'm steve ducey i'm  brian killme and i'm ainsley earhart and  click here to subscribe to the fox news  youtube page to catch our hottest  interviews and most compelling analysis
 

